1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,300
Claude Sheets,

2
00:00:01,310 --> 00:00:02,360
2026 beta:

3
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:02,805
you think checking

4
00:00:02,815 --> 00:00:04,800
AI numbers will cost you a redo,

5
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:06,448
but actually formulas show how.

6
00:00:06,698 --> 00:00:07,310
Here's how,

7
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,345
on our hiring budget:

8
00:00:09,355 --> 00:00:10,610
three teams, four quarters.

9
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,355
Before, in our example,

10
00:00:12,365 --> 00:00:14,030
you pasted Claude's chat table

11
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,440
into another tool:

12
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,560
three totals, just text,

13
00:00:16,570 --> 00:00:17,674
no formulas.

14
00:00:17,924 --> 00:00:19,415
Checking meant redoing the math;

15
00:00:19,425 --> 00:00:20,890
Claude had no live access

16
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:21,721
to your edits.

17
00:00:21,971 --> 00:00:23,830
Now, in the paid-plan beta,

18
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,545
the spreadsheet stays in Claude;

19
00:00:25,555 --> 00:00:27,447
you both edit the same cells.

20
00:00:27,697 --> 00:00:29,430
Claude's formulas stay in the cells,

21
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,810
so you can check how each number

22
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:31,960
was calculated:

23
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,130
if our total skipped a quarter,

24
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:35,243
its formula shows it.

25
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:37,550
Claude's edits are
outlined as they land,

26
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,535
so you see them;

27
00:00:38,545 --> 00:00:39,925
when it finishes,

28
00:00:39,935 --> 00:00:41,910
a card can undo just those edits,

29
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,851
but only briefly.

30
00:00:43,101 --> 00:00:44,420
So, what we learned:

31
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,750
pasted, our three totals
hid their math;

32
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,165
in the paid-plan beta,

33
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:49,707
they're formulas you can check.

34
00:00:49,957 --> 00:00:50,740
Want more?

35
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,290
Subscribe, and comment

36
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,147
what we should explain next.
